# TypeScript Frontend Code Quality Rules

- Prefer simple and readable code over clever one-liners.
- Use early returns to reduce nesting and keep render/logic flows clear.
- Keep logic DRY; extract repeated transformations and guards into shared helpers/hooks.
- Use descriptive names; prefix event handlers with `handle` (for example: `handleSubmit`, `handleRowClick`).
- Prefer immutable update patterns for arrays/objects in state and derived data.
- Avoid `JSDoc` for basic TypeScript-typed functions; rely on strong type definitions.

## Example
```ts
if (!user) return null;
if (!user.isActive) return <InactiveUserBanner />;
```
